#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "This defines which contributions will be considered for synchronisation by defining a time frame. This is optional"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can enter any valid strtotime() expression like \"2017-01-01\" or \"now - 2 days\"."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Last processed membership ID"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Membership Number Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can select a membership custom field to contain the Membership Number"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The field has to be an active, alphanumeric (text) type, is_view, searchable custom field to be eligible."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Show in Summary View"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "If you select this, the current membership number of the contact will be show in the contact's summary view, underneath the external identifier."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Number Pattern"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "If you fill this field the membership number will automatically generated for new memberships."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Any characters are allowed but it is advisable to stick to alphanumeric characters, and to avoid whitespaces and special characters."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Additionally, the following special tokens are currently available: {mid[+offset]} for the CiviCRM Membership ID and {cid[+offset]} for the CiviCRM Contact ID, each with an optional offset value, e.g. {mid+1000} or {cid+100000}."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Cancel Date Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The core membership entity only has an end date, but if you want to keep track of the date somebody cancelled the membership, you can create a new custom field of type Date. You can then select it here to make this date available as a token."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Cancel Reason Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The core membership entity doesn't have a field for the cancel reason, but if you want record this data, you can create a new custom field of type Text. You can then select it here to make this date available as a token."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Payment Contract (paid via) Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can select a membership custom field to record the connection to any recurring contribution, e.g. a CiviSEPA mandate or similar."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The field has to be an integer type, active, read only, and searchable custom field to be eligible."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Annual Amount Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Select an editable monetary field where you define the annual expected membership fees, should they deviate from the amount defined by the membership type."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Record annual fee changes"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "If active, any change of the annual amount (determined by the two fields above) will be recorded as an activity."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "End with Statuses"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "For any membership status you select, the linked recurring contribution or mandate will be ended automatically should a membership be set to that status."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Hide Auto Renewal"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The built-in auto renewal feature interferes with the P60 membership concept, so we recommend not to use it. If you activate this option the fields will be hidden from the UI and the column in the tab and the search result will be freed up for something else."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Extend membership when contribution is completed"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Extend the membership as soon as the membership contribution is set to completed."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "This will calculate the new end date and a new status."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Remark: This only works if there is exactly one contribution per membership period."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Installment Amount Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Select a read-only monetary field to display the installment amount as provided by the paid-via recurring contribution."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Annual Gap Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Select a read-only monetary field to display any deviation between annual amount as required and as provided by the paid-via recurring contribution."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Payment Frequency Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can choose any select field, but its options have to have entries for the following values: 1 (monthly), 3 (quarterly), 6 (semi-annually), 12 (annually)."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Payment Type Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Pick a field to reflect your recurring contribution's payment instrument. You can simply use the built-in payment_instrument group, or specifiy a mapping below."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Payment Type Field Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can enter a string to map the payment instrument id of your recurring contribution in the field above to the values of your option group."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The format is a comma separated list of \"payment_instrument_id:option_group_value\" mappings, e.g. \"1:3,2:2,5:4,6:4\"."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Missing Amount (current period)"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Holds the outstanding amount for the current membership period. This is calcualted by the Membership.process job."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Only Synchronise From"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Only Synchronise Until"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Backward horizon (in days)"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "If a membership payment is received within this number of days before the current starting date, the start and the join date will be extended to the payment's received date."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Grace Period (in days)"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Membership payments will be accepted up to this amount of days after the current end date."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "In order to associate contributions with expired memberships, you will first have to manually extend those memberships."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Paid by Field"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "You can select a membership custom field to indicate that another contact is paying for this membership."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "The field has to be an contact reference type, active, and searchable custom field to be eligible."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Live Statuses"
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Only if a membership has a 'live' status, membership payments will be assigned to it."
msgstr ""

#: settings/membership.setting.php
msgid "Caution: This status list is only valid for the payment synchronization tool, the membership extension job uses the parameter status_ids instead."
msgstr ""

